        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Identify the stain, match the solvent to it, and let the poultice dry out completely. Three or four patient cycles will clear marks that no amount of scrubbing would have touched — and scrubbing would have dulled the polish on the way.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Then reseal the patch, because a stain is evidence that the stone was absorbing. The removal fixes today's mark; the sealing is what stops you doing this again next month in the same spot.
          </p>
